# SEO and indexing

Use this when changing public pages, document head metadata, sitemaps, or indexing.

The authenticated dashboard stays out of search indexes. `noindex` those routes and leave them out of `sitemap.xml`.

- Each public URL has one title and one meta description.
- Canonical URLs use the production origin the owner has confirmed. Do not invent a domain.
- Open Graph and Twitter card metadata point at a real social image.
- Structured data describes only content the page actually shows.
- `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, and `llms.txt` are required for the public site and absent today.
- The heading outline has one `h1`. Internal links use real routes.

Detail is in `docs/quality/seo.md`. Audit with the `seo-audit` skill.
